# Vulnerabilities accepted after analysis. Each entry records who accepted it, when, why, and until
# when: after the expiry date the CI image scan fails again, so an acceptance cannot be forgotten.

# CVE-2026-47884 (CRITICAL), spring-webmvc: remote code execution via improper path limitation in
# XsltView. Fixed only in Spring Framework 7.0.9 (Spring Boot 4); there is no fix in the 6.2 line.
# Accepted by: Payments Integration squad, 2026-11-20.
# Not exploitable here: payment-intake has no view layer. The code defines no XsltView, view
# resolver or template engine (none are auto-configured), and its endpoints read the body as byte[]
# and answer empty bodies or application/problem+json.
# Plan: migrate to Spring Boot 4 before the expiry (technical debt #9 in practical/README.md).
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-03-31

# CVE-2026-47890 (CRITICAL), spring-webmvc: stream corruption in Server-Sent Events rendered with
# views. Fixed only in Spring Framework 7.0.9 (Spring Boot 4); there is no fix in the 6.2 line.
# Accepted by: Payments Integration squad, 2026-11-20.
# Not exploitable here: the code uses no Server-Sent Events, no streaming responses (SseEmitter,
# ResponseBodyEmitter, StreamingResponseBody) and no views. Every response is a single, empty or
# application/problem+json body.
# Plan: same migration to Spring Boot 4, same expiry.
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-03-31
